# Nova Agent Development Rules

## ALWAYS Load Context First
Before any code changes or analysis:
1. Load `docs/flattened-codebase.xml` - Contains the latest codebase snapshot
2. This file is automatically updated on every commit
3. If the file seems outdated, run: `npm run update-context`

## Core Rules
- Follow all rules in `.cursor/rules/00-nova-agent.md`
- Apply BMAD planning from `.cursor/rules/01-nova-agent-bmad-planning.md`
- Check agent-specific rules in `.cursor/rules/bmad/`

## Context Management
The flattened codebase is automatically:
- Deleted and recreated on each commit (to save space)
- Updated with latest code changes
- Optimized to include only essential files
- Referenced by all BMAD agents

## Quick Commands
```bash
# Manual update if needed
npm run update-context

# Watch for changes
npm run watch-context

# Plan new features
npm run new-feature -- --feature <name>
```

## Important Paths
- Context: `docs/flattened-codebase.xml`
- Rules: `.cursor/rules/`
- Planning: `docs/planning/`
- Scripts: `scripts/`
